INT. ICE HARVESTER GALLEY - SATURN RING ORBIT - NIGHT

Frost on every surface. Red strobe. The hull groans.

ADAEZE (40s, flight engineer, burn-scarred hands) jams a pry bar into a sealed hatch. TOBIAH (20s, rookie, suit two sizes too big) holds a failing lamp. MIRA (30s, medic) counts breaths off a wrist display.

KOZLOV (50s, captain, grey stubble) slaps a dead console. Nothing.

A small shape in the vent grate. SENNA (14, stowaway, hollow-eyed) watching.

TOBIAH
Pressure's dropping. Forty percent.

ADAEZE
Hold the light still!

MIRA
Who is that? In the vent?

KOZLOV
Not now, Mira.

TOBIAH
Thirty-five!

ADAEZE
Then stop talking and pull!

MIRA
Kid. Kid, come out.

SENNA
It's behind the wall.

KOZLOV
Both of you, quiet.

Silence. Scratching inside the bulkhead. Moving. Fast.

KOZLOV
We leave. Now.

ADAEZE
Hatch isn't open!

SENNA
It heard you.

The bulkhead BUCKLES. Everyone freezes.

TOBIAH
I'm not going first!

MIRA ^
I'm taking the kid!
